SUMMARY:Third Kumārila Conference
DESCRIPTION:From Monday May 18\, 2026 to Friday May 22\, 2026\, the third Kumārila conference will take place at Maanjiwe Nendamowinan\, 1535 Outer Circle\, University of Toronto Mississauga. \nKumārila is one of the rare thinkers who are truly irreplaceable. Sanskrit philosophy would not have been the same without his contributions to epistemology (e.g.\, his epistemology of absence\, of linguistic communication\, his theory of intrinsic justification…)\, philosophy of action\, deontics\, hermeneutics and ontology. Still\, his work is partly untranslated and largely understudied. A group of scholars started meeting in 2024 with the shared purpose of studying Kumārila and making him accessible to scholars of philosophy. As a result of the first two Kumārila conferences\, a reader on Kumārila will be published by OUP at the end of 2026. During this third conference scholars will translate\, analyse and discuss new passages by Kumārila in 2- or 3-hours sessions. Younger scholars (including students) will also be invited to the conference and will deliver shorter talks. \nSpeakers will include Kei Kataoka\, Lawrence McCrea\, Monika Nowakowska\, Andrew Ollett\, Akane Saito\,  Taisei Shida\, Kiyotaka Yoshimizu. \nPreliminary program \nMonday May 18th (Kumārila’s Ślokavārttika 1)\nChair: John Nemec\n8.30 onwards: Breakfast\n9–10 Alessandro Ganassi\, The final argument from Śūnyavāda’s pūrvapakṣa: how the nature of things can be contradictory (ŚV\, sūnyavāda)\n10–10:15 Tea break\n10:15-11:15am Zihao Wu\, Toward a more comprehensive understanding of svataḥprāmāṇya: suspension of awareness beyond temporal sequence\n11:15–11:30 Tea break\n11:30–12:30 Devansh Bharadvaj\, Kumārila on the perception of the self (ŚV\, ātmavāda)\n12:30–1:30 Lunch break\nChair: Daniele Cuneo\n1:30–4: Taisei Shida\, Ślokavārttika Śabdādhikaraṇa vv. 1–19b & 163c–201b\n4-4:15: Tea break\n4:15-5:15: Alessandro Graheli\, abhihitānvayavāda in Kumārila\, Mukula\, Jayanta \nTuesday May 19th (Kumārila’s Ślokavārttika 2; Kumārila’s Tantravārttika 1)\nChair: Manasicha Akepiyapornchai\n8:30 onwards: Breakfast\n9–10: Sarju Patel\, svataḥprāmāṇya in Kumārila and Bhāsarvajña\n10–10:15 Tea break\n10:15–12:45: Andrew Ollett\, āgnēyyadhikaraṇa (TV ad 3.2.8)\n12:45–1:45 Lunch break\nChair: Ajay Rao\n1:45-4:15pm: Nilanjan Das\, Kumarila on the meaning of common nouns (TV ad 1.3.30–35)\n4:15–4:30: Tea break\n4:30–5:30: Aaron Minnick\, Kumarila on caste (TV ad 1.2.2) \nWednesday May 20th (Kumārila’s Tantravārttika 2)\nChair: Elisa Freschi\n8.30 onwards: Breakfast\n9–10: Nirali Patel\, Kumārila has his yogic cake and eats it: Kumārila on ātmatuṣṭi (TV 1.3.adh.7)\n10–10:15 Tea break\n10:15–12:45: Alessandro Graheli\, Kumārila on Grammar in the vyākaraṇādhikaraṇa (TV 1.3.adh. 9)\n12:45–1:45 Lunch break\n1:45–4:15: Walk in the park \nThu May 21st (Kumārila’s Tantravārttika 3)\nChair: Munena Moiz\n8.30 onwards: Breakfast\n9–10 Kiyotaka Yoshimizu\, Nitya or Kāmya from the Mīmāṃsā Viewpoint (TV ad 2.4\, adh. 1)\n10-10.15: Tea break\n10.15–12:45: Monika Nowakowska\, upāṃśuyājādhikaraṇa (TV ad MS 2.2.9-12)\n12:45-1:45pm Lunch break\nChair: Jesse Pruitt\n1:45-4:15pm: Larry McCrea\, vacanavyakti from Grahaikatvādhikaraṇa (TV ad 3.1.7\, pp. 705-709 in the Anandashrama 1st ed.)\n4:15-4:30: Tea break\n4:30—5:30: Akane Saito\, Theories of Error in Medieval Indian Philosophy\, with special focus on Kumārila \nFri May 22nd (Kumārila’s Tantravārttika 4\, Kumārila’s Ṭupṭīkā)\nChair: Shashank Rao\n8:30 onwards: Breakfast\n9–11:30: Kei Kataoka\, The Definition of a Single Sentence in Kumārila’s Tantravārttika: A Translation of the Ekavākyatālakṣaṇādhikaraṇa (TV 2.1.46)\n11:30–11:45: Tea Break\n11.45–12.45: Elisa Freschi What is the thing to be done in “the one desirous of heaven should sacrifice”? (ṬṬ ad 6.1.1–3)\n12:45-2:15: Lunch break\nChair: Nilanjan Das\n2:15-4:45pm: Akane Saito\, śeṣatvasya lakṣyanirdeśādhikaraṇa and teṣāmarthādhikaraṇa (TV ad MS 3.1.3-6\, 7-10) \n6pm: Dinner together
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/third-kumarila-conference/
LOCATION:Maanjiwe nendamowinan\, 1535 Outer Circle Road\, Mississauga
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George,UTM,UTSC
END:VEVENT
